<p>HardPoint is arranged in six areas, named for the job: <strong>Home</strong>, <strong>Sell</strong>, <strong>Customers</strong>,
  <strong>Stock</strong>, <strong>Buy</strong> and <strong>Reports</strong>. You only see the areas your role uses, and only the
  features your shop has switched on (see <a href="#features">Switching features on and off</a>).</p>

<h2>The top bar</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The areas are along the top. The one you're in is highlighted, and its own menu is underneath: in Stock, for example,
    <strong>Products</strong>, <strong>Stock levels</strong>, <strong>Reorder</strong>, <strong>Stock takes</strong>,
    <strong>Transfers</strong> and <strong>Expiry</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>Search</strong> (or <strong>Ctrl K</strong> anywhere) finds products, customers, suppliers, receipt and order numbers, and pages,
    even by the names they used to have. Scan a barcode into it to open that product.</li>
  <li><strong>Open till</strong> takes you straight to the point of sale, for those who sell.</li>
  <li>The <strong>gear</strong> opens Settings.</li>
  <li>Your name, on the right, opens <strong>My profile</strong> (password, PINs, two-factor, the daily email), <strong>Switch user</strong>,
    <strong>Help</strong>, <strong>Contact support</strong> and signing out.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Home</h2>
<p>Owners and managers see today's takings, sales, margin and cash in the drawers, then <strong>Needs you today</strong>: low stock,
  overdue customers and suppliers, stock takes to approve, orders to collect and deliveries to send, each with the button that deals
  with it. Cashiers see one big button into the till, with their own sales underneath.</p>

<h2>Where things moved</h2>
<p>If you used HardPoint before the six areas: Products, Inventory and the stock side of Purchase are now <strong>Stock</strong>;
  the reorder list and reorder suggestions are one <strong>Stock › Reorder</strong> page; customers, jobs and who owes us are
  <strong>Customers</strong>; promotions and deliveries are in <strong>Sell</strong>; supplier invoices are on
  <strong>Buy › What we owe</strong> and returns to suppliers on <strong>Buy › Purchase orders</strong> (the ⚙ menu); categories, brands,
  units, tax rates, price lists, staff and activity are in <strong>Settings</strong>. Old links still work and take you to the new page.</p>

<h2>Searching and filtering lists</h2>
<p>Lists such as Products, Sales, Orders &amp; quotes and Purchase orders have a search bar at the top.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Type a few letters of a name, SKU, receipt or order number and press Enter. A barcode scanner works in the search bar too.</li>
  <li>The small arrow at the end of the bar opens <strong>Filters</strong>: a branch, a status, a date and so on. Each filter you choose
    shows in the bar as a tag; press its <strong>×</strong> to remove it.</li>
  <li>Long lists are split into pages; use <strong>‹</strong> and <strong>›</strong> on the right.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Group By</h2>
<p>On <strong>Stock › Products</strong>, <strong>Buy › Purchase orders</strong> and <strong>Sell › Orders &amp; quotes</strong>, the same dropdown has
  a <strong>Group By</strong> column. Grouping turns the list into one row per group with how many it holds and their total:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Products by <strong>category</strong> or <strong>brand</strong>;</li>
  <li>Purchase orders by <strong>supplier</strong> or <strong>status</strong>, to see what's still to come from each supplier;</li>
  <li>Orders and quotes by <strong>status</strong> or <strong>customer</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Open a group to see what's in it. Filters and search still apply, so "Open orders, grouped by customer" works. Choose the grouping again
  to switch it off.</p>

<h2>Settings</h2>
<p><strong>Settings</strong> collects everything you set up once: shop details, billing, features, branches and tills; M-Pesa, Airtel
  Money, KRA eTIMS, SMS and currencies; staff and activity; and the catalogue's categories, brands, units, tax rates and price
  lists. Reports has the QuickBooks export.</p>

<h2 id="features">Switching features on and off</h2>
<p>Owners choose what their shop uses in <strong>Settings › Features</strong>: deliveries, promotions, foreign
  currencies, the online store, contractor jobs, batches and expiry dates, serial numbers, and the API. A feature that's
  off is left out of the menus, Settings, Home and forms. Nothing is deleted, so switching it back on brings everything back.
  A feature can't be switched off while it's live (a promotion running, products recording batches); the page says what to finish first.</p>

<h2>Getting help</h2>
<p><strong>Help</strong> opens these guides. If you're stuck, <strong>Contact support</strong> (under your name) sends us a message with the
  page you were on, so we can see what you see. Or chat with us on WhatsApp.</p>
